  "question": {
    "text": "If the number of ways in which four distinct balls can be put into two identical boxes such that no box remains empty is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Every ball has two options<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>4</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math> balls can be put in <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></math> ways.<br /><br />Arrangement among themselves is&nbsp;<math><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></math><br /><br />So, total ways<math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />But, above count also includes the one case in which all the balls are put in one box,<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi></math> required number of ways&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>",
    "image": null
  },
